  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-50 (not deemed medically necessary), which is a substantive denial rather than a coding or administrative error, so resubmitting the same data (submit_clean) or fixing codes (correct_and_resubmit) will not resolve the medical necessity issue. The payer does not offer peer-to-peer review, and retroactive authorization is not available, leaving a formal appeal as the only viable path to challenge the medical necessity determination. Historical data shows that while success rates are mixed, appeals are the standard and only effective mechanism for overturning CO-50 denials in this context.",
